{
  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" State of Madhya Pradesh versus Ramkumar Choudhary pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2024','2024_11_1280_1288','2024INSC932'); ><font size='4'> <strong>STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>RAMKUMAR CHOUDHARY </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 11 S.C.R. 1280</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2024 INSC 932</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010006982024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : J.B. PARDIWALA, R MAHADEVAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Appellant-State challenged the High Court judgment dismissing the second appeal filed with an inordinate delay of 5 years holding that the delay was not explained satisfactorily. Headnotes&dagger; Delay &ndash; Refusal to condone &ndash; When justified &ndash; Delay of 5 by the appellant-State &ndash; Not condoned by High Court, appeal dismissed &ndash; Challenged: Held: High Court rightly refused to condone the delay &ndash; Enormous delay occurred at every stage, from the date of receipt of the judgment passed by the First Appellate Court till the date of filing<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 29-11-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> SPECIAL LEAVE PETITION (CIVIL) No. 48636/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2024','2024_11_1280_1288','2024INSC932','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0',